Open Econ Agent
===============

This project is a local-first adaptation of EconAgent that runs the
macroeconomic LLM-agent simulation on open-source models via Ollama.

It builds on two prior works:

1. EconAgent (ACL 2024)
   "EconAgent: Large Language Model-Empowered Agents for Simulating
   Macroeconomic Activities."
   Nian Li, Chen Gao, Mingyu Li, Yong Li, Qingmin Liao. ACL 2024.
   Repository: https://github.com/tsinghua-fib-lab/ACL24-EconAgent

   The LLM-agent layer of this project (the decision prompts, the
   dialog/reflection loop, and the composite baseline) is derived from
   the EconAgent implementation. Open Econ Agent adapts it to local open
   models and adds tolerant response parsing and configuration.

2. Foundation / The AI Economist (BSD-3-Clause)
   Zheng, Stephan, et al. "The AI Economist: Improving Equality and
   Productivity with AI-Driven Tax Policies." arXiv:2004.13332 (2020).
   Repository: https://github.com/salesforce/ai-economist

   The economic simulation core vendored under `ai_economist/` is the
   Foundation framework, licensed BSD-3-Clause. Its original per-file
   copyright headers are preserved, and its BSD-3-Clause license text is
   included at `ai_economist/LICENSE` (Copyright (c) 2020, salesforce.com,
   inc.). That license governs everything under `ai_economist/`.

